 // fighters sorted by y
 ...
 // texts
 ctx.restore();
 // vignette screen
 ...
 // announcements / pause
}
```
Note background screen fill uses view; drawArena covers -600..bottom. For portrait with oy maybe ~245, top screen corresponds -295; arena covers. Fine.

Sort fighters by y: larger y (closer) drawn later. Currently y is depth; player y 0. For same y, draw player first? Doesn't matter. Maybe enemy on right overlaps gloves.

Particles and texts after fighters in world coordinates.

Announcements:
```
if(announce>0&&running){const a=Math.min(1,announce*2);...}
```
announce counts down from 2.4. Text "RONDA 1" for announce>0.9, "¡PELEA!" for <0.9. Use font size scaled to min(w*0.1, 64). Good.
Also draw "ÁRBITRO" no need; remove.

Pause overlay screen "PAUSA / Toca ▶ para continuar".

Result UI covers.

Vignette screen radial.

Also add top cinematic letterbox? no.

Camera scale issue: fighter x 250..710; portrait half=235 (w 390,s .83 -> half 235); camX clamped 240..720? I set 240..720; mid e.g. 480. If both fighters at 250 and 710 mid 480, view 245..715 → both visible. At extremes, one fighter at 250 with camX 480 → visible 245..715, just visible. Good. If both near 250 mid 250, camX clamp 240 → view 5..475, both at 250. fine.

Wide half>480 => camX 480.

Let me replace render.

